    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17849" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτο-πάθεια</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰ], ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one's own experience,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ αὐ. διατίθεσθαι τοὺς λόγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.108.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδιοπάθεια</span>
			, <i>primary affection,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.78
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm., of
			words that are <i>reflexive,</i> opp. transitive, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				147.21
			</span></i>.</div>
